          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Lagrangian submanifold
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            is a submanifold which is a maximal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropic+submanifold"} isotropic submanifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            on which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            vanishes, and which is maximal with this property.
          %p
            In the archetypical example of an even dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{R}^{2n}
            equipped with its canonical symplectic form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega = \sum_{i = 1}^n d q_i \wedge d p^i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{2n}
            of fixed values of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{q_i\}_{i = 1}^n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            = succeed "," do
              %em locally
          %p
            Lagrangian submanifolds are of central importance in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            where they constitute
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaves"} leaves
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+polarizations"} real polarizations
            and are closely related to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
          %p
            If one thinks of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"} canonical momenta
            (= parameterization of a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaf"} leaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinate"} canonical coordinate
            (= parameterization of
            = succeed ")\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaf+space"} leaf space
          %p
            A Lagrangian submanifold equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half-density"} half-density
            is a model for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
            of the physical system in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiclassical+approximation"} semiclassical approximation
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BatesWeinstein"} Bates-Weinstein, p. 14
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
            (see there) is a refinement of this concept.
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A (
              %strong Lagrangean
              or)
              %strong lagrangian submanifold
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \hookrightarrow X
              such that the following equivalent conditions hold
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  at each point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \in L
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi ℓ
                        %mi L
                        %mo ↪
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi ℓ
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_\ell L \hookrightarrow T_\ell X
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+subspace"} Lagrangian subspace
                  (hence a simultanously
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropic+subspace"} isotropic subspace
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coisotropic+subspace"} coisotropic subspace
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi ℓ
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_\ell X
                  equiiped with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_x
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \hookrightarrow X
                  is a maximal
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropic+submanifold"} isotropic submanifold
          #LambdaStructures.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              More generally one can consider Lagrangian submanifolds of symplectic structures in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroids"} symplectic Lie n-algebroids
              equipped with their canonical
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomials"} invariant polynomials
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifolds"} dg-manifolds
              (via their
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
                \-structures
              in (
              %a{:href => "#Severa"}> Ševera, section 4
              ).
          %h2#examples_in_higher_differential_geometry Examples in higher differential geometry
          %p
            We discuss classes of examples of Lagrangian dg-submanifolds, remark
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LambdaStructures"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroids"} symplectic Lie n-algebroids
          %h3#OfAPoissonLieAlgebroid Of a Poisson Lie algebroid
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{P}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            as the algebra of functions on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"} dg-manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          #ForPoissonLieAlgebroidyByLagrangianFoliation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A dg-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifold"} Lagrangian submanifold
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              is a Lagrangian dg-submanifold, also called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
                  \-structure
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Severa"} Ševera, section 4
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
              by such
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaves"} leaves
              is a Lagrangian
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+of+a+Lie+algebroid"} foliation of a Lie algebroid
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \pi)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
              underlying a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔓
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              corresponds to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coisotropic+submanifold"} coisotropic submanifold
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \pi)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Severa"}> Ševera, section 4
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              As a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              with bracket structure, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔓
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{P}
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi T
                              %mo *
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi π
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T^* X &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\pi}{\to}&amp;&amp; T X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              where the horizontal morphism is given by contraction/pairing with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+tensor"} Poisson tensor
            %p
              It is sufficient to consider this locally over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
              and hence we set without essential restriction of generality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{R}^n
              with the
              = succeed "/graded" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{P})
              being
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∧
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega = \mathbf{d} x^i \wedge \mathbf{d} p_i
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{q_i\}_{i = 1}^n
              are the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              and where the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p_i\}
              are the canonical coordinates on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi T
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*_x \mathbb{R}^n \simeq \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              Consider then a sub-Lie algebroid of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔓
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{P}
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi T
                              %mo *
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; T^* X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    S &amp;\hookrightarrow &amp; X
                    }
            %p
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+subspace"} Lagrangian
              with respect to the above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              consists of precisely those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+vectors"} cotangent vectors
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which vanish when evaluated on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vectors"} tangent vectors
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi N
                      %mo *
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E = N^* S
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conormal+bundle"} conormal bundle
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi N
                      %mo *
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi T
                      %mi S
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N^* S \hookrightarrow T^*_S X
              of vector bundles is an inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              precisely if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anchor+map"} anchor map
              restricts to an anchor on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              lands in tangent vectors of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi N
                      %mo *
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi(N^* S) \subset T S
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is the standard definition for what it means for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coisotropic+submanifold"} coisotropic submanifold
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The dg-Lagrangian submanifolds also correspond to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
              (see there) on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔓
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
          %h3#OfACourantLie2Algebroid Of a Courant Lie 2-algebroid
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+algebroid"} Courant Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℭ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
